<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 19794 0 R/Alt(Two diagrams. (a) Two lanes that face each other, the RTL (gold) on top and the netlist (gate) below. In each lane, the inputs a, b, and c enter a large shaded triangle, the cone of r.D, which narrows to its tip at the D input of a register r. In the RTL, the cone holds an AND gate of a and b, followed by an OR gate with c. In the netlist, it holds a NAND gate of a and b and an inverter on c, followed by a second NAND gate. A smaller triangle, the cone of y, holds an XOR gate of the register output r.Q and of c, which reaches it on a long wire around the lane, and narrows to its tip at the output y. Dashed red lines with an equals sign connect the tips of the two cones of r.D and the tips of the two cones of y, labeled compare r.D and compare y. A dotted grey line connects the outputs of the two registers, labeled matched r.Q: same free value. (b) A bus r.Q, c of width 2 splits to a blue triangle, the gold cone of y, and a green triangle, the gate cone of y. Their tips drive the two inputs of a red XOR gate, whose output diff goes to a box with the question solver: can diff be 1 for any input? Below it: no means the cones are equal, yes means a counterexample.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 31963 0 R>>
endobj
