20293 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 20294 0 R/Alt(Gate-level circuit diagram. On the left, the input D drives the upper input of a NAND gate and, through an inverter, the lower input of a second NAND gate below it. The gate input G drives the lower input of the upper NAND gate and the upper input of the lower NAND gate. The output of the upper gate, S bar, drives the upper input of a third NAND gate, whose output is Q. The output of the lower gate, R bar, drives the lower input of a fourth NAND gate, whose output is Q bar. A dashed box labeled SR latch encloses the third and fourth gate. Q feeds back to the upper input of the fourth gate and Q bar to the lower input of the third gate, and the two feedback wires cross between the gates.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 31972 0 R>>
endobj
