20337 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 20338 0 R/Alt(Two panels. (a) Circuit diagram. A dashed box labeled D flip-flop contains two orange latch boxes, the master latch on the left and the slave latch on the right, each with the pins D, G, and Q. The input D drives D of the master, Q of the master, named qm, drives D of the slave, and Q of the slave is the output Q. The clock clk drives the gate G of the master through an inversion bubble and the gate G of the slave directly. Under the master, the note says transparent while clk = 0, under the slave transparent while clk = 1. (b) Timing diagram over four clock periods with the rows clk, D, qm, and Q. The phases where clk is low are shaded. D rises in the first low phase, falls in the second high phase, shows a short pulse in the third high phase, and rises again in the third low phase. qm rises with D in the first low phase, falls at the start of the second low phase, ignores the pulse, and rises with D in the third low phase. Q changes only at the rising edges: high from the second, low from the third, and high from the fourth edge on.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 31973 0 R>>
endobj
