<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 24878 0 R/Alt(Gate-level circuit. Input c drives an inverter whose output, marked with a red cross and s-a-0, drives one input of a NAND gate. Input d drives the other NAND input. Inputs b and a drive an OR gate. The NAND and OR outputs drive a NOR gate with output y. Values are written on the wires: c 0, inverter output 1/0, d 1, NAND output 0/1, a 0, b 0, OR output 0, y 1/0. The values with a slash are red and mark the path of the fault.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 32036 0 R>>
